From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 22:43:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 08/44] minimize: live preview capture as a tested state
 machine

The compositor raises duplicate_frame when the next frame is created
before cctk has destroyed the previous one, which happens only after its
ready or failed handler returns. Every commit already went through a
timer; move the decision of when to allocate, commit, arm the timer or
stop into a pure state machine (pacing.rs) with no Wayland types, so the
rule is checked by tests: ready and failures never commit directly, and
no sequence of up to six events commits with a frame in flight.

Behaviour is unchanged, except that after a buffer-constraints failure
the old buffer is kept until the new constraints replace it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
